# 🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (measured 2026-08-28 on the published tarball).
# `files: ["src", ...]` in package.json includes everything that sits on disk under
# src/ — and the repo's root .gitignore does NOT apply here: npm looks for an ignore
# file inside the package directory, finds none, and ships the lot. That is how
# src/.claude/hooks/ — our own session state, logs and hook config — travelled into a
# public package for anyone to download. Gitignored is not npmignored.
src/.claude/
.claude/

# Sidecar tables of contents are generated for our own reading, not for the product.
*.toc
